.\" Simple Shell man page
.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "February 2025" "Version 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- Simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple shell that reads and executes commands from standard input.
.PP
Features:
- Executes commands with arguments
- Handles PATH environment variable
- Works in both interactive and non-interactive modes
- Only forks when command exists
- Handles spaces and empty lines
.SH OPTIONS
No options are currently supported.
.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive mode:
.RS
$ ./hsh
#cisfun$ /bin/ls
#cisfun$ ls -l /tmp
#cisfun$ exit
.RE
.PP
Non-interactive mode:
.RS
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
PATH is used to find executables.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Isgandarov Vusal
